Waiver comment : Reviewed intentional unconnected output ports in the integrated SoC: unused optional interface signals, unused FIFO status/usage outputs, unused arbiter indices and read-enable outputs. Functional data, control and handshake paths remain connected.
waive -rule "W287b" 
#spg_backref : "./spyglass_lint_final/novacrypt_spyglass_final/soc_top/lint/lint_rtl/novacrypt_spyglass_final_waiver_file.awl" 21

Waiver comment : Reviewed unused input signals across the integrated SoC, including unused AXI/APB sideband fields, optional test and flush controls, unused CPU interface inputs and vendor FIFO/arbiter inputs. These signals are not required by the implemented functionality.
waive -rule "W240" 
#spg_backref : "./spyglass_lint_final/novacrypt_spyglass_final/soc_top/lint/lint_rtl/novacrypt_spyglass_final_waiver_file.awl" 22

Waiver comment : Reviewed multiple assignments in procedural blocks across SoC integration, CPU pipeline, Wallace multiplier, CSR, AXI interconnect, FIFO, GPIO, PLIC, CLINT and peripheral logic. Assignments implement intentional default values, conditional overrides, loop-based aggregation and priority updates. Existing assignment ordering is intentional and preserves functional priority.
waive -rule "W415a" 
#spg_backref : "./spyglass_lint_final/novacrypt_spyglass_final/soc_top/lint/lint_rtl/novacrypt_spyglass_final_waiver_file.awl" 23

Waiver comment : Intentional unused GPIO subregister write-enable outputs; register data paths remain connected and hardware does not require these write strobes.
